  partName: Intake Manifold (3)
  description: The Intake Manifold (3) is a small, complex metal component positioned
    at the middle-center-center of the jet engine, responsible for distributing air-fuel
    mixture to the engine's combustion chambers. Its metal-dark material provides
    a high level of thermal insulation, minimizing heat transfer and optimizing engine
    performance. Interestingly, the intake manifold's complex shape is designed to
    maximize airflow and minimize pressure losses.
